  "result": "{\"seen_before\": false, \"matches\": [], \"answer\": \"I couldn't find a past ticket that reports this exact crash. It's a PowerToys Run (PowerLauncher) exception: `InvalidOperationException: Operation is not valid while ItemCollection has no inner collection`. It's thrown from `MainWindow.ViewModel_PropertyChanged` while the window is loading (`OnLoaded` → `set_MainWindowVisibility`). The archive does have other PowerToys Run crashes. Examples are #10094 (collection modified during startup) and #6954 (index out of range from a race on the results list). Those have different stack traces and different causes, so they aren't the same problem. To get this one investigated, please do the following. 1) Restart PowerToys, or end the PowerLauncher process in Task Manager, and see if it recurs. 2) Update to the latest PowerToys release. 3) Send a bug report ZIP (tray icon → Report bug) and the PowerToys Run logs from %localappdata%\\\\Microsoft\\\\PowerToys\\\\PowerToys Run\\\\Logs. 4) Tell us whether it happens on every start or only occasionally, and what you were doing when it happened. 5) Give the ticket a descriptive title and fill in the expected and actual behaviour.\"}",
